---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/08-11/', spec='https://www.lpkf.com/fileadmin/mediafiles/user_upload/products/pdf/DQ/flyer_lpkf_protomat_s104_en.pdf', manual='https://www.manualslib.com/manual/2570966/Lpkf-Protomat-S64.html?page=';
---
<Layout pageTitle="LPKF ProtoMat S104 · artwork inspection" description="Inspect connectivity and an inaccessible isolation gap in an inert two-net teaching coupon." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment pm"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/08-11/">← Equipment 08-11</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#pm-evidence">Sources and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">08-11 · GEOMETRIC ARTWORK CHECK / FIRST PASS</span><h2>LPKF ProtoMat S104</h2><p>Inspect an inert two-net copper coupon and check whether a circular gauge fits the narrowest gap. The 3D fixture is an inspection prop. It does not move the spindle or generate machining commands.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Enclosed fixture</h3><div id="pm-view" aria-label="Orbitable S104 enclosure; move the display hood to inspect the stationary spindle, 20-position rack and vacuum table"></div><div class="bar"><button data-pm-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-pm-view="platen">Vacuum table</button><button data-pm-view="rear">Rear</button><button id="pm-hood">Open display hood</button></div><p id="pm-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Orbit and zoom using drag and pinch or scroll. The blue handle moves the display hood; the turquoise head marker runs the same geometric check as the button.</p></section>
<section><h3>Two-net artwork</h3><p>Loaded: <output id="pm-loaded">BTS-08-11-INERT-001 · coupon-r1</output></p><div class="fields"><label>Circular reference gauge diameter (mm)<input id="pm-diameter" type="number" value=".8" min=".05" max="5" step=".001"/></label><label>Import v1 rectangular coupon (JSON)<input id="pm-input" type="file" accept="application/json,.json"/></label></div><div class="bar"><button id="pm-inspect" class="primary">Inspect copper artwork</button><button id="pm-example">Restore example</button></div><p id="pm-status" aria-live="polite">The default coupon contains a 0.35 mm gap. Inspect with the 0.8 mm reference gauge, then try 0.25 mm to see the classification change.</p><canvas id="pm-map" width="730" height="440" aria-label="Top view of the inert rectangular coupon with two copper islands and closest gap marked"></canvas></section></div>
<section><h3>Connectivity and clearance</h3><output id="pm-result">No inspection result.</output><div class="bar"><button id="pm-export" disabled>Export report JSON</button></div><p>The reported connection map is ideal top-layer geometry, not a circuit measurement. The report does not certify that a path exists through the gap.</p></section>
<section id="pm-evidence"><h3>Model and evidence</h3><p>Selected reference: enclosed S104 with standard integrated vacuum table and 20-position rack; no optional dispenser or external accessories. Reconstructed from the <a href={spec+'#page=1'}>LPKF front three-quarter flyer photo</a>, <a href={manual+'30'}>manufacturer manual V1.0 p. 30 (working area)</a>, <a href={manual+'31'}>p. 31 (side/rear)</a> and <a href={manual+'32'}>p. 32 (head)</a>. Links preserve the original illustrations; no vendor photograph is reproduced below.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="650" height="450" src={base+'inside.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original open cutaway showing head, table, bellows and tool rack"/><figcaption>Original open cutaway compared with the flyer and manufacturer p. 30 for control area, platen, rack and bellows. Transparent hood hidden in this render for clarity.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="650" height="450" src={base+'rear.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original rear rendering of closed hood and connector area"/><figcaption>Original rear render compared with p. 31. Overall connector area placement is referenced; port geometry and spacing are approximate.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Specification or check</th><th>Reference</th><th>Actual / model use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Enclosure W × H × D</td><td>680 × 560 × 800 mm, flyer p. 2</td><td>GLB envelope matches nominal values; remaining geometry inferred.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Nominal layout / rack</td><td>305 × 229 × 8 mm / 20 positions, flyer p. 2</td><td>Hardware context only. Inspection accepts 2–100 mm rectangular coupons and assumes no Z processing.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Two intended nets</td><td>Exactly two disjoint connected islands; NET_A holds A1 and A2</td><td>2/2; literal rectangle graph verified.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Known local gap</td><td>44.35 − 44.00 = 0.35 mm</td><td>0.350 mm within 0.000001 mm numerical tolerance. 0.8 mm too narrow; 0.35 mm gives zero margin; 0.25 mm has local width available.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Inputs are one top copper layer, the rectangular outline, 2–80 labeled copper rectangles, two declared nets and a circular reference diameter (0.05–5 mm). Artwork coordinates use the lower-left board origin in mm, +X right and +Y away. Geometry is checked on a 1 µm coordinate grid; exact shared boundaries are ideal electrical contact, including point contact. Use the downloadable example for the format. Other layers, out-of-outline shapes, unknown pads, invalid coordinates and unsupported files are rejected. Industry PCB file formats are not accepted.</p>
<p>For each axis, use the positive separation between the two closed rectangle intervals; then compute pair distance as <code>√(Δx² + Δy²)</code>. Join copper rectangles whose distance is zero, compare components with the intended pad map, and compare the cross-net distance with the reference diameter. This gives connectivity and <strong>local width only</strong>, not an accessible tool path, copper removal, electronics, calibration or fabrication-ready revision. Output preserves unchanged artwork, sample and pad IDs, revision, contact groups, closest points and clearance in mm.</p>
<p><a href={base+'example-artwork.json'} download>Example input</a> · <a href={base+'example-report.json'}>Output contract example</a> · <a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={base+'protomat-s104.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No hardware, downstream reader or headset support is claimed.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/08-11/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.pm{max-width:76rem}.pm .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.pm section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin:.8rem 0;padding:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.pm .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.45rem;margin:.6rem 0}.pm .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.5rem}.pm label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2em;font-size:.93rem}.pm button,.pm input{min-width:0;max-width:100%;min-height:2.4em;padding:.34em .52em;font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.13rem}.pm button{cursor:pointer}.pm button:disabled{opacity:.55;cursor:default}.pm .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.pm #pm-status.error{color:#a54a34}.pm #pm-view{height:clamp(270px,32vw,420px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.pm #pm-view :global(canvas){display:block;width:100%;height:100%}.pm #pm-map,.pm img{width:100%;height:auto}.pm #pm-result{white-space:pre-line;font-family:monospace;display:block}.pm figure{margin:.75rem 0}.pm table{font-size:.9rem;border-collapse:collapse}.pm th,.pm td{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.pm .scroll{overflow:auto}@media(max-width:800px){.pm .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
